{
    "background_story": "Lincoln was a majestic coucal bird known for his striking black plumage and distinctive call. He lived in the dense rainforests of Southeast Asia, where his unique song could be heard echoing through the trees. Lincoln was a solitary creature, but he had a special bond with a local ornithologist named Dr. Maria. She had been studying the coucal population for years, and Lincoln had grown accustomed to her presence. Every morning, he would fly down to her campsite, singing his sweet melody as if to greet her. Dr. Maria marveled at Lincoln's intelligence and adaptability, and he became an integral part of her research. As the years passed, Lincoln became a symbol of the rainforest's beauty and resilience, and Dr. Maria's work helped protect his habitat for generations to come.",
